// Cultures: who built a settlement (draft 108 of the design wiki, P57a; see
// crates/worldgen/src/settlements/culture.rs and docs/settlements.md).
//
// FAMILIES. The world is cut into regions about `rules.field.cell` blocks across (Voronoi
// cells on a jittered grid). Each cell names one family: the one most of its sample points
// suit by `biome` tag (fully) or `half` tag (at half weight) and `temperature` (°C, a hard
// range), times the family's `weight` and a bit of luck. So neighbours share a family, and
// one biome holds different peoples in different parts of the world. Within
// `rules.field.border` blocks of a cell's edge a settlement mixes in a share of the next
// cell's family. `claim: Water` families (river folk) take a place by its site instead,
// where fresh water is near and trade runs high, and the region's family becomes the
// second; `claim: City` ones (the Old Empire) are given out by P57c for cities only.
//
// A family is a bundle of leanings:
//   axes      its mean on eight axes, each 0 ..= 1: piety, martial, trade, craft, festivity,
//             outlook, hierarchy, lore. A settlement draws its own from this, a regional
//             drift, local noise and shifts from its site (see the wiki's Towns tab). Any
//             `lean` in settlements.ron may name an axis as well as a lever.
//   tilt      what it favours (above 1) or shuns (below 1; 0 removes) in settlements.ron's
//             lists: styles, houses, roofs (Gable, Hip ...), props, centrepieces, layouts,
//             extras (Chimney, Porch ...), each by name. A tilt multiplies the entry's own
//             weight.
//   palette   its eight colours as blocks, for walls, trim and roofs; a settlement keeps
//             three to five and adds them to its style's, as `rules.palette` times the
//             style's own weight. `{wood}` and `{trim}` as in styles.
//   quirks    how much it favours some quirks (below), by name.
//   names     the parts of its places' names, each with its Japanese reading. `script: Kana`
//             joins them by the `kana` table of settlements.ron; `Kanji` runs them together.
//             First and last parts, small words for hamlets, prefixes (which may lean on
//             levers or axes).
//
// MUTATION. Each settlement drops 1 to 3 of its family's favourite entries (fewer where
// order is high), borrows 0 to 2 favourites from its second family or a random one (about
// outlook x trade x 3 of them), keeps three to five of its eight colours, and has a quirk
// (one in four places a second): so no two places of a family are alike.
//
// QUIRKS. A small oddity: its `lean` on levers and axes (how likely it is), what it needs
// of the ground (`need`: Relief, Water), a shift of the axes and its own tilt. Several of
// the wiki's quirks show most once P57b and P58 land (doors, cats, kites); until then their
// tilt only leans the lists.
//
// Every name in a tilt must be in settlements.ron's lists; loading fails otherwise.
(
    rules: (
        field: (cell: 6144, jitter: 0.8, probes: 3, border: 512.0, share: (0.45, 0.1)),
        luck: 0.6, luck_cell: 18432, smooth: 0.08, claim: (0.35, 0.55),
        drift: (2048, 0.12), local: 0.1,
        drop: (1, 3), borrow: 2, borrow_scale: 3.0, keep: (3, 5), second_quirk: 0.25,
        palette: 0.5,
        site_shift: {
            "age": (piety: 0.15, lore: 0.1), "wealth": (hierarchy: 0.15),
            "order": (lore: 0.1), "forest": (craft: 0.05),
            "water": (trade: 0.15, outlook: 0.1), "green": (festivity: 0.1),
            "martial": (festivity: -0.1, outlook: -0.2), "trade": (outlook: 0.3),
        },
        size_shift: {
            "town": (martial: 0.05, trade: 0.05, hierarchy: 0.1),
            "city": (martial: 0.1, trade: 0.1, hierarchy: 0.2),
        },
        level_martial: (3, 0.06), level_piety: (7, 0.1),
    ),
    families: [
        (
            name: "hearth", title: ("Hearthfolk", "炉辺の民"), weight: 1.5,
            biome: ["grassland", "temperate", "lush", "flowers"], half: ["forest", "broadleaf", "cool", "warm"], temperature: (2.0, 24.0),
            axes: (piety: 0.5, martial: 0.3, trade: 0.5, craft: 0.5, festivity: 0.6, outlook: 0.6, hierarchy: 0.4, lore: 0.4),
            tilt: (
                styles: {"timber_frame": 2.0, "birch_cottage": 1.2},
                houses: {"cottage": 1.4, "farm_house": 1.6, "long_house": 1.2, "barn": 1.5, "mill": 1.5, "wing_house": 1.2, "chapel": 1.2, "bakery": 1.3},
                roofs: {"Gable": 1.3, "HalfHip": 1.4},
                props: {"HayBale": 1.5, "ChickenCoop": 1.6, "FenceRun": 1.4, "Scarecrow": 1.6, "Cart": 1.3, "FlowerBed": 1.3},
                centrepieces: {"Maypole": 1.8, "GreatTree": 1.4, "Windmill": 1.6, "DuckPond": 1.5, "MarketCross": 1.4},
                layouts: {"green": 1.8, "street": 1.2, "ring": 1.2},
